High-Level Design of Modular AI Assistant System:

1. User Interface Layer (GUI/Web Frontend): The user interface serves as the primary point of interaction between users and our AI assistant, which provides accessibility across devices like mobile phones or computers with web browsers. Here are some crucial components for this layer: 
   - Responsive design to ensure a seamless experience on different screen sizes;
   - Accessible navigation menu that allows the user to explore various functions of our AI assistant easily, such as setting preferences, adding tasks or questions promptly;
   - Customization options for users so they can personalize their interactions with us. 

2. Core Service Layer: This layer contains all business logic and back-end processes essential to the functioning of our AI assistant system without which it could not operate effectively, such as accessing databases or third-party APIs that provide additional information required for providing user assistance; this includes but is not limited to:
   - NLP engine (Natural Language Processing) – responsible for understanding and responding to the queries using contextual data provided by users. The integration of state-ofde-the-art deep learning models like GPT, BERT or T5 can be explored; 
   - Knowledge graph construction & management tools that maintain a constantly updated repository containing facts on various topics which our AI assistant could draw knowledge from when needed to provide informative responses. This layer should support dynamic updates and integration of external data sources as necessary for expanding the scope or content domain, if required; 
   - Task Automation Framework – this module performs automated tasks assigned by users without needing any human intervention whenever possible (like setting reminders) to improve efficiency and user experience. This component would rely on scheduling algorithms that ensure appropriate timings for completing these actions based upon the time of day or when a specific event is anticipated;
   - Data Management – this subsystem ensures secure, reliable handling/storage of sensitive data gathered from users during interaction to respect privacy laws and regulations (e.g., GDPR) while also providing necessary access for system maintenance purposes only with proper authorization mechanisms in place such as multi-factor authentication or role-based access control;
   - External API integration – this service enables the AI assistant's ability to communicate effectively with external services, like weather information providers. These APIs can be used when users ask specific questions related to them and enable real-time data retrieval from these sources without having our system maintaining its own internal databases or servers;
   - Notification System – this subsystem is responsible for alerts/reminders delivery ensuring tasks are accomplished as per user's requirements. This could also be extended into the ability to send notifications when relevant updates occur on specific topics of interest maintained in knowledge graphs, etc.; 

3. Data Management Layer: Responsible for handling large volumes and velocity data generated by users during interactions with our AI assistant system; this includes but is not limited to storage (on-premises or cloud platforms), backup & recovery mechanisms as well as providing scalability/flexibility options based on demands.

4. Monitoring Layer: Essential for ensuring the overall health and stability of our AI assistant system; this layer includes real-time monitoring tools that provide insights into performance metrics, usage patterns, error logs or any other information indicating potential issues within various components/subsystems in their operation with automatic alert systems.

5. Security Layer: Ensures the confidentiality and integrity of user data by implementing secure communication protocols like SSL/TLS to safeguard against unauthorized access; it also includes mechanisms such as authentication (multi-factor or role-based), authorization controls, encryption during storage & transmission for sensitive information while adhering with regulations regarding GDPR and other local data protection laws.

6. Integration Layer: Acts as the bridge between different subsystems within our AI assistant system by integrating diverse APIs from various external sources which can provide additional capabilities to improve user experience or functionality, like weather information providers etc., while also ensuring these third-party services are reliable and maintain good performance metrics.

7. Reporting Layer: Responsible for providing insights into system analytics such as response times, error rates; this can be invaluable to developers during debugging sessions or assessment of overall efficiency/performance while also being helpful for users with respects to understanding how quickly they might receive responses from the AI assistant.

8. Maintenance & Support Layer: Dedicated team responsible for regular system updates, bug fixes and improvements as well as user support via FAQ sections or a direct contact option (live chat/email). This layer also includes training resources for developers in improving existing functionalities based on users' feedback or trends.

To ensure seamless interoperability between all layers of our modular AI assistant system, we would implement service-oriented architecture principles with RESTful API design along with message queues and load balancers to manage high loads efficiently while maintaining a consistent user experience across different devices/platforms.
